# Public.com API Credentials
# ==========================
# Obtain your API key from: https://public.com/api
#
# Place your API key in the environment variable: PUBLIC_API_KEY
#
# Example export (bash):
#   export PUBLIC_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
#
# Example PowerShell:
#   $env:PUBLIC_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
#
# The API key is passed as an Authorization header.
# Do not share your API key publicly.

# Schwab API Credentials (optional, for cross-validation)
# Obtain these from the Schwab developer portal
# Place these in your local .env file (not this example):
#   SCHWAB_APP_KEY=your_app_key_here
#   SCHWAB_SECRET=your_app_secret_here
#   SCHWAB_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_refresh_token_here
#
# Example PowerShell:
#   $env:SCHWAB_APP_KEY="your_app_key_here"
#   $env:SCHWAB_SECRET="your_app_secret_here"
#   $env:SCHWAB_REFRESH_TOKEN="your_refresh_token_here"
#
# These are used only by the Schwab adapter in cross-validation.
# Do not share your credentials publicly.